title: No confidence vote against the new government
subtitle: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] faces a vote of no confidence.
new-page: true
view-if: bruning_event_timer = 5 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not traditionalist_split_2 and not kvp_formed and not bourgeois_coalition >= 50 and not concord_formed
on-arrival: bruning_event_seen = 1; judicial_reform -= 1
tags: event
max-visits: 1

= Vote of no confidence

Following the collapse of our coalition, President [+ president +] has appointed Heinrich Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] Party in a government supported by bourgeois forces. However, they cannot survive without the support from us or the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. 

Askew, has reorganized his cabinet to include the parties to the right of the [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if not lvp_formed and not gold_exist: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], such as the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> and let the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> take over as Minister of Agriculture, presumably to pressure the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to support his government. We are left with the choice to "tolerate" the government to prevent the gains of extremists within the Assembly or vote to oust Askew for new elections.

- @vote_no
- @vote_no_nothing
- @vote_yes
- @vote_yes_nothing

@vote_no
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there will be new elections.
view-if: right_coalition < 50
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 3; bruning_event_timer = 0; unionist_relation -= 5
call: set_next_election_time

We have broken with the [+ chancellor +] government, and have voted against them in a vote of no confidence. We also repealed their emergency powers. Westmore and his group of moderates that still remain within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> are outraged with Mallin letting the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> takedown [+ chancellor +]'s right-wing government, and resign en masse.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@vote_no_nothing
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: Askew looks to the right.
on-arrival: traditionalist_bruning = 1; unionist_relation -= 5
view-if: right_coalition >= 50

We have broken with the [+ chancellor +] government, and have voted against them in a vote of no confidence. However the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> surprisingly votes in favor with the government, preventing new elections from being called.

Their support of the cabinet is unreliable, with Mallin at the helm. It's a matter of time before a crisis takes down the cabinet.

@vote_yes
title: Oppose the vote of no confidence, voting for the government.
subtitle: We would essentially provide "toleration" to a bourgeois government.
view-if: right_coalition < 50
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; commons_marcher *= 0.9; disfavored_marcher *= 0.9; disfavored_royalist += 5; disfavored_collectivist += 5; commons_royalist += 5; commons_collectivist += 3; commons_marcher -= 4 if welfare < 0; disfavored_marcher -= 5 if welfare < 0; pro_republic -= 4; collectivist_relation -= 8; ddp_left += 1; gold_left += 1; lvp_left += 1; other_r += traditionalist_r*0.4 if not kvp_formed; kvp_r += traditionalist_r*0.4 if kvp_formed; traditionalist_r = traditionalist_r*0.6; landed_traditionalist -= 4; burgher_traditionalist -= 4; guild_traditionalist -= 4; landed_other += 4 if not kvp_formed; burgher_other += 4 if not kvp_formed; guild_other += 4 if not kvp_formed; landed_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; burgher_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; guild_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; traditionalist_split_2 = 1; traditionalist_split_2_timer = 1 if not kvp_formed

We try to convince the workers that this policy is necessary in order to maintain a stable parliamentary government, and to deal with the fiscal consequences of the depression. Still, this policy provides excellent recruiting fodder for <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>.

Westmore and his group of moderates that still remain within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> are outraged with Mallin letting the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> influence the [+ chancellor +] right-wing government, and resign en masse[? if kvp_formed:&nbsp;to join the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?].

@vote_yes_nothing
title: Oppose the vote of no confidence, voting for the government.
subtitle: The bourgeois rather work with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> over allowing us to influence government.
on-arrival: traditionalist_bruning = 1; unionist_relation -= 5
view-if: right_coalition >= 50

This has become unnecessary with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> surprisingly voting in favor of the government, preventing new elections from being called.

Their support of the cabinet is unreliable, with Mallin at the helm. It's a matter of time before a crisis takes down the cabinet.
